    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d670">

                <pb facs="0774" n="672" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg672"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.119/281: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Reinsch</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-09-10T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 10,
                                1919, 5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Your August 30, 5 p.m. Department has interpreted your 2760 of May 19,
                        1919,<anchor n="99" xml:id="d670-f1"/> as including raw material for
                    manufacture of arms and ammunition and has only recently held it to include the
                    machinery used in their manufacture.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d670-f1" n="99" xml:id="d670-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; substance conveyed to the Department by despatch No. 2725, of May
                    10, <ref target="#pg669">p. 669</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
